# Testing and regression

Previously working payment behaviour is never assumed unaffected. UI/chat/poll changes can break payments. Payment architecture is **PRODUCTION-FROZEN** — full suite before any allowed payment-system exception.

## Commands

- Fast (iteration): `npm run test:payments:fast`
- Full (before payment completion): `npm run test:payments:full`
- Live-flag source guard: `npm run test:live-guard`
- Release-oriented: `npm run test:sourcebridge`

Do not duplicate test logic — aggregators invoke existing `scripts/test-*.mjs`. Fast/full suites must **not** create Stripe network financial objects.

## Generic users

Core automated tests: User A / B / C. Permutations: A proposes A-buyer/B-sourcer; A proposes B-buyer/A-sourcer; B proposes A-buyer/B-sourcer; B proposes B-buyer/A-sourcer. Historical usernames only in explicit fixture blocks.

## What full covers

Ticket create/roles/accept/revise/cancel/isolation, 3-active, fees, Protected, Direct Destination Charge, sourcing funding authorization (no charge), procurement, fulfilment, receipt, 12h inspection, issue hold, final release, completed state, poll reconciliation, cross-user viewer isolation.

Manifest: `docs/PAYMENT_REGRESSION.md`.
